  "owner_review": "Integration coordinated exact-head #540 merge, reviewed the UDP wire gate and syscall ownership, and coordinated the private guest and release.",
  "runtime_scope": {
    "option": "The SDK SOL_SOCKET/SO_BROADCAST int is a kernel-owned Boolean on the native IPv4 UDP endpoint, initially zero and shared by descriptor aliases.",
    "gate": "With the option disabled the kernel returns EACCES for 255.255.255.255 and the local /24 directed broadcast before autobind and ARP. Applies at send time, including connected, nonblocking message and native UDP paths.",
    "wire": "Enabled broadcast goes directly to ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff. The peer and pcap verified eight enabled broadcast datagrams and two ordinary unicast datagrams across two runs. No denied payload or broadcast ARP appeared. All ten IPv4 headers passed checksum verification.",
    "scope": "UDP connect records a peer. Option checks happen when sending. The current IPv4 receive filter admits local unicast and limited broadcast. DHCP has a separate internal transmit path."
  },
